  "problem": "A manufacturing company has three sites, factory $1,$ factory $2,$ and factory $3.$ They all produce two light bulb types: A and B.\n\n- Factory $1$ produces $25%$ of the entire production, and $2%$ of those bulbs are defective.\n\n- Factory $2$ produces $50%$ of the entire production, and $3%$ of those bulbs are defective.\n\n- Factory $3$ produces $25%$ of the entire production, and $1%$ of those bulbs are defective.\n\nIf $40%$ of all light bulbs are of type A, and $1%$ of type A light bulbs are defective, what is the probability that a randomly chosen defective light bulb is of type A? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
